 "text": "9/29/26, 9:48 AM\n\nAnalyze Incoming Payments\n\nWith the Analyze Incoming Payments (F5588) app, you can monitor and analyze incoming payments to optimize clarification\nprocesses and team workload.\n\nKey Features\nYou can use this app to regularly do the following:\n\ne Analyze how many payments have been clarified manually within a given period.\n\ne Analyze the effectiveness of the automated clarification process provided by the standard.\n\n1 Note\n\nIf you have licensed and are using SAP Cash Application, add-on for contract accounting, you can regularly validate the\neffectiveness of the applied machine learning to the clarification process.\n\nYou display the data per company code. You can refine the filter criteria as required by choosing Adapt Filters to include, for\nexample, the posting date, and lot type.\n\nThe app analyzes payment lots, credit lots, and check lots, and displays an overview of which amount and number of payments in a\npayment lot has been cleared automatically or manually.\n\n1 Note\n\nIf you are using SAP Cash Application, add-on for contract accounting, the app analyzes payment lots, credit lots, and check\nlots, and displays an overview of which amount and number of payments in a payment lot has been cleared using machine\nlearning.\n\nViews\n\nYou can display the data by using the following view options:\n\ne The Chart View shows all payment lots matching the filter criteria.\n\nThe default dimension is Lot. The default measures are Payments in Clarification, Payments Posted Automatically,\nPayments Posted Manually, and, if you are using SAP Cash Application, add-on for contract accounting, Payments Posted\nUsing Cash App.\n\ne The Table View lists more details per payment lot than the Chart View, including the total number of payments in\nclarification, the total number of items in lots, and the total payment amount in the last row of the table.\n\nYou can combine the table and chart view in a single display.\n\nFor each view, you can change chart, dimensions, and measures in the Settings dialog. You change the display by selecting a chart\ntype in combination with a dimension and measures.\n\n(e)\neo Eyamnla\n",
